{"task_id": "17", "solution": "def square_perimeter(side_length: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculate the perimeter of a square.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    side_length : float\n        The length of one side of the square. Must be positive.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    float\n        The perimeter of the square, calculated as 4 * side_length.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    ValueError\n        If side_length is not positive.\n    \"\"\"\n    if side_length <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"side_length must be a positive number\")\n    return 4 * side_length"}
{"task_id": "18", "solution": "def remove_chars(s1: str, s2: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return a copy of `s1` with all characters that appear in `s2` removed.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s1, str):\n        raise TypeError(f\"s1 must be str, got {type(s1).__name__}\")\n    if not isinstance(s2, str):\n        raise TypeError(f\"s2 must be str, got {type(s2).__name__}\")\n\n    if not s2:\n        return s1\n\n    remove_set = set(s2)\n    result_chars = [c for c in s1 if c not in remove_set]\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)"}
