{"task_id": "75", "solution": "def filter_divisible(tuples_list: list[tuple[int, ...]], k: int) -> list[tuple[int, ...]]:\n    \"\"\"Return a list of tuples where every element in each tuple is divisible by k.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    tuples_list : list[tuple[int, ...]]\n        List of tuples containing integer elements.\n    k : int\n        Divisor; must be a positive integer.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    list[tuple[int, ...]]\n        Tuples that satisfy the divisibility condition.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    TypeError\n        If k is not an int, if any element in tuples_list is not a tuple,\n        or if any element in a tuple is not an int.\n    ValueError\n        If k <= 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(k, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"k must be an integer\")\n    if k <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"k must be a positive integer\")\n\n    result: list[tuple[int, ...]] = []\n\n    for t in tuples_list:\n        if not isinstance(t, tuple):\n            raise TypeError(\"All items in tuples_list must be tuples\")\n\n        for elem in t:\n            if not isinstance(elem, int):\n                raise TypeError(\"All elements in tuples must be integers\")\n            if elem % k != 0:\n                break\n        else:\n            result.append(t)\n\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "77", "solution": "def is_divisible_by_11(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Check if an integer is divisible by 11.\n\n    This function accepts an integer (positive, negative, or zero) and returns\n    True if the number is evenly divisible by 11, otherwise False.  Non\u2011integer\n    inputs will raise a TypeError.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    n : int\n        The integer to test for divisibility.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    bool\n        True if n % 11 == 0, False otherwise.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    TypeError\n        If n is not an instance of int.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be an integer\")\n    return n % 11 == 0"}
