{"task_id": "98", "solution": "def average_product(numbers: list[float]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the average of the product of a list of numbers.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    numbers : list[float]\n        A non\u2011empty list of numeric values (int or float).\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    float\n        The product of all numbers divided by the length of the list.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    ValueError\n        If 'numbers' is an empty list.\n    TypeError\n        If any element in 'numbers' is not int or float.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list must not be empty.\")\n    product: float = 1.0\n    for value in numbers:\n        if not isinstance(value, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(f\"All elements must be numeric; got {type(value).__name__}.\")\n        product *= float(value)\n    length: int = len(numbers)\n    return product / length"}
{"task_id": "99", "solution": "def decimal_to_binary(n: int) -> str:\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non\u2011negative integer\")\n    if n == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n    bits = []\n    while n:\n        bits.append(str(n % 2))\n        n //= 2\n    return \"\".join(reversed(bits))"}
