{"task_id": "240", "solution": "def _get_element_type(lst):\n    \"\"\"Return the type of the first element of the list, or None if the list is empty.\"\"\"\n    return type(lst[0]) if lst else None\n\ndef _validate_inputs(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"Validate that both arguments are lists and satisfy the preconditions.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(list1, list) or not isinstance(list2, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both arguments must be of type list.\")\n\n    if len(list1) == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"list1 must contain at least one element.\")\n\n    type1 = _get_element_type(list1)\n    type2 = _get_element_type(list2)\n\n    # If both lists are non-empty, check that their element types match.\n    if type1 is not None and type2 is not None and type1 != type2:\n        raise ValueError(\"Elements of list1 and list2 must be of the same type.\")\n\ndef replace_last_with(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Replaces the last element of list1 with all elements of list2, modifying list1 in place.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    list1 : list[object]\n        The list whose last element will be replaced. Must be non-empty.\n    list2 : list[object]\n        The list whose elements will replace the last element of list1.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    TypeError\n        If either argument is not a list.\n    ValueError\n        If list1 is empty.\n        If the element types of list1 and list2 are not compatible.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_inputs(list1, list2)\n\n    # Remove the last element of list1\n    list1.pop()\n\n    # Extend list1 with the elements from list2\n    list1.extend(list2)"}
