{"task_id": "793", "solution": "def find_last_occurrence(arr: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Find the last index of `target` in a sorted list `arr`.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    arr : list[int]\n        Sorted (ascending) list of integers.\n    target : int\n        The value to locate.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    int\n        Index of the last occurrence of `target`, or -1 if not found.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    TypeError\n        If `arr` is not a list or `target` is not an int.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(arr, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"arr must be a list\")\n    if not isinstance(target, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"target must be an int\")\n    if not arr:\n        return -1\n\n    low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == target:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif arr[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    return result"}
